 "contract": {
  "input_location": "registers",
  "input_arrangement": "packed_striped",
  "output_location": "smem",
  "output_form": "indices",
  "output_sorted": false,
  "temp_storage_bytes": 0,
  "sync_assumed": "the whole hardware warp calls the primitive together (all logical warps at once), as the harness does",
  "sync_performed": "shuffles, ballots and one any-vote over the full hardware warp, no barrier",
  "type_constraints": "bf16 keys only, one row of N keys per call packed as bf16x2 words (the harness's packed_striped arrangement, items 2 (j LW + lane) and 2 (j LW + lane) + 1 in word j), the even items form set A in the low halves and the odd items set B in the high halves, one more bitonic merge on one-key words after the SIMD network, int32 source indices derived from the position. fp32 keys unsupported",
  "nan_behavior": "a NaN key is never selected (it loses every max.bf16x2 and min.bf16x2 against a number and both set.gt and set.eq are false), so with fewer than k non-NaN keys output slots stay unwritten. Focus-set inputs carry no NaN. -0.0 equals +0.0: the network orders -0.0 below +0.0, the recovery classifies by IEEE comparison, the selected set is the oracle's set in every case (signed_zero pattern passes under both requirements). Denormals compared as values",
  "tie_break_support": "both unsorted requirements with the same code: the tie class at the k-th key fills the remaining slots, in index order whenever it has to be capped (prefer_smaller_index exact by construction), measured identical throughput under both requirements in every cell",
  "sorted_output_support": "none: the greater class is written in lane order, then the tie class (lane order on the common path, index order on the capped path). A sorted output would need one shuffle per selected key to move the recovered index to its network position",
  "k_range": "[1, N / 2] with MaxK = round_up(k, LW) dividing N / 2, measured k 4, 16, 32, 64",
  "n_range": "N = 2 x LW x words with (N / 2) / MaxK a power of two, N at least 64 at LW 32 (N 32 unsupported, each set would hold fewer keys than lanes), measured N 64 to 256"
 },
 "correctness": {
  "oracle_passed": true,
  "cases": 286,
  "notes": "unsupported N5_split_f__W1x_vimnmx_eager__bf16_T32_N32_K4_not_guaranteed | unsupported N5_split_f__W1x_vimnmx_eager__bf16_T32_N32_K4_prefer_smaller_index | unsupported N5_split_f__W1x_vimnmx_eager__bf16_T32_N32_K16_not_guaranteed | unsupported N5_split_f__W1x_vimnmx_eager__bf16_T32_N32_K16_prefer_smaller_index | Oracle battery (13 cases) passed on every cell under both requirements. Control W1x_vimnmx_eager (the T42 one-word min max network) in the same lock section, final commit 8f613a317f (batch b3), the development batches b1 (ops_sel, 3ede7791e3) and b2 (ops_bf16, 30f5b8f821) under state/results/opt-N5/. N 32 cells are unsupported by the contract (listed under unsupported). prefer_smaller_index and not_guaranteed share the common path but compile to different kernels in the fast form (the exact ballot fallback is compiled in for prefer_smaller_index, the capped prefix for not_guaranteed), and the prefer_smaller_index kernel carries 3 to 16 more registers and runs 2 to 4 percent slower in throughput in most cells (up to 9 percent at LW 8 N 128), a T28 schedule and register effect of code that never executes on random input. The exact form compiles the same code for both requirements and measured identical throughput to 0.1 percent."
 },
